Vendored Arm "mlw" weight-codec decoder
=======================================

This directory contains an imported copy of the Ethos-U "mlw" (machine-learning
weight) entropy decoder, used by hw/npu/ethos_u_weights.c to decompress the
Vela-compiled weight stream that the guest hands to the modelled Ethos-U NPU.

Provenance
----------
  Project: Arm ethos-u-vela (NXP downstream fork)
  Source:  https://github.com/nxp-imx/ethos-u-vela
  Branch:  lf-6.12.49_2.2.0
  Path:    ethosu/mlw_codec/{mlw_decode.c,mlw_decode.h,mlw_common.h}
  License: Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory and the per-file headers)

Only the *decoder* is imported. The matching reorder (weight traversal) and
scale/bias packing are NOT vendored: their inverse is reimplemented as QEMU's
own GPL-2.0-or-later code in hw/npu/ethos_u_weights.c, and validated against the
reference Python module (ethosu.mlw_codec) by tests/unit/test-ethos-u-mlw.c
using vectors committed under tests/data/ethos-u/ (regenerate with gen.py).

Local modifications
-------------------
Kept as small and as clearly marked as possible so re-importing stays easy:

  mlw_decode.c
    - includes "qemu/osdep.h" instead of the individual libc headers;
    - a bitstream underrun sets an error flag and unwinds gracefully (returning
      a short/empty result) instead of printf()+exit(1), so malformed guest
      data cannot terminate the QEMU process;
    - the slice/chunk loops bail out once that error flag is set.
  The decode algorithm itself is byte-for-byte identical to upstream.

  mlw_decode.h
    - newly written here (the upstream header is not part of the import set);
      declares only int mlw_decode(...).

Hardening note
--------------
The decoder still contains a handful of assert()s guarding bitstream invariants
(palette/GRC-divisor ranges). The caller in ethos_u_weights.c length-checks the
decoded weight count against the value expected from the command stream and
rejects a mismatch; tightening these asserts into soft errors is tracked for the
upstream submission.
